<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pratapsinh Gaekwad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1908">1908</a>–<a href="/years/1968">1968</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Pratapsinhrao Gaekwad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pratapsinh Gaekwad was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Baroda, succeeding his grandfather <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayajirao-gaekwad-iii">Sayajirao Gaekwad III</a> in 1939. He acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947, and in 1949 Baroda was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a>. The Indian government withdrew its recognition of him as Maharaja in 1951, transferring the title to his son.</p></div>
